   "kind": "rejection",
   "at": "2026-11-09",
   "title": "Tried: sessions wrote memory edges with relations outside the seven the graph knows (informs, implements, refines, supports …) or with from/to keys. What broke: merge-inbox printed 'skip edge' and carried on, the file moved to merged/, and context.mjs --check still passed. 229 of 3,062 inbox edges never reached the graph; 25 of the 96 well-formed ones are 'supersedes', so replaced decisions still read as current. Do not rely on an edge having merged; the merger should fail on an unknown relation and the check should compare merged-inbox edges with the graph."
  },
